# L §5.5 Naming the options: "Otherwise it prints the options that give it, joined by ` | ` (rate_reading =
# down | half-up), and the line's reading: entry names the same options (§8.2)."  Three options, two of which
# give one value: v[o1] = v[o3] = 1, v[o2] = 2.  The line of a set sorts at its first option's place.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2016-03-01
  start 2015-11-01
  end 2016-10-31

source s "s"

axis rr
  o1 "one"
  o2 "two"
  o3 "three"

input v[a in rr]: int

version x
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2016-01-01
  v[o1] = 1
  v[o2] = 2
  v[o3] = 1

ask q1: v[rr]
=== expect
q1 [rr = o1 | o3]: 1
  reading: rr = o1 | o3
  cut 2016-03-01
q1 [rr = o2]: 2
  reading: rr = o2
  cut 2016-03-01
